---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NextDollarLab from "../../components/NextDollarLab.tsx";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import RegionNote from "../../components/RegionNote.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your Next Dollar: Order of Operations"
  description="Where should the next dollar go — pay down debt, grab the match, fund a Roth, or invest in a brokerage? Check off what you've done and see the single next step in the priority ladder, and why it ranks there."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Personal Finance · Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>Where should your next dollar go?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Match? Debt? Roth? Brokerage? The order you fund things in matters more than
      most single investment choices — capturing a 50% employer match beats any
      stock pick. Check off what you've handled and see the one next step, and the
      logic that puts it there.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <RegionNote>
      US-focused — this ladder is built around US accounts (employer 401(k) match,
      HSA, IRA, Roth vs. Traditional). The underlying logic — free money, then
      guaranteed returns, then tax-advantaged space, then taxable — generalizes
      anywhere, but the account names and limits are American.
    </RegionNote>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <NextDollarLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this order?</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Free money first.</strong> An employer match is an instant,
          guaranteed return no investment can match. Leaving it on the table to do
          anything else is almost always a mistake.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Then guaranteed returns.</strong> Paying off high-interest debt
          earns you a risk-free return equal to its rate. Clearing a 20% card beats
          any return you can reliably expect from the market.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Then tax-advantaged space.</strong> HSAs, IRAs, and 401(k)s
          shelter your growth from tax — a durable, compounding edge. That space is
          limited each year, so it's worth filling before the taxable account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Then the taxable account.</strong> No limits, fully flexible, and
          the natural home for anything left once the sheltered space is full.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This is a sensible default, not a personalized plan: a very low-rate
        mortgage, a Roth 401(k) match, or a specific goal can reshuffle the middle.
        For the account-choice details, see the
        <a href="/personal-finance/retirement-accounts">Retirement Accounts tool</a>.
        Educational only, not financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="next-dollar" />

  <section class="container pf-related">
    <h2 class="pf-related-heading">Keep exploring</h2>
    <ul class="grid grid--2 pf-related-grid">
      <li>
        <a href="/personal-finance/debt-payoff" class="card">
          <h3>Clear the high-interest debt first</h3>
          <p>The ladder puts high-rate debt near the top. Compare avalanche vs. snowball and see months to debt-free.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/personal-finance/retirement-accounts" class="card">
          <h3>Which account, and how much</h3>
          <p>Once the order is clear, dig into the account choices themselves: Roth vs. Traditional and the employer match.</p>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro { padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md); max-width: var(--measure-wide); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--color-text-soft); line-height: 1.5; }
  .wl-explainer { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
  .pf-related { margin-top: var(--space-xl); }
  .pf-related-heading { font-size: var(--step-1); padding-bottom: var(--space-xs); border-bottom: var(--border); margin-bottom: var(--space-md); }
  .pf-related-grid { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .pf-related-grid a.card { height: 100%; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; display: block; }
  .pf-related-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 0.3rem; font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .pf-related-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step--1); }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .nd-ladder {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }
  .nd-step-btn {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color var(--transition), background var(--transition);
  }
  .nd-step-btn:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: var(--color-accent); }
  .nd-step-btn:disabled { cursor: default; }
  .nd-step-mark {
    flex: none;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 1.7rem;
    height: 1.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .nd-step-body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; min-width: 0; }
  .nd-step-label { font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .nd-step-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }
  .nd-step-detail {
    margin: 0.3rem 0 0.2rem 2.4rem;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  /* Status styling */
  .nd-step--done .nd-step-mark { background: var(--color-accent-soft); color: var(--color-accent); }
  .nd-step--done .nd-step-label { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .nd-step--current .nd-step-btn {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }
  .nd-step--current .nd-step-mark { background: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-surface); }
  .nd-step--current .nd-step-tag { color: var(--color-accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .nd-step--upcoming .nd-step-btn { opacity: 0.75; }
  .nd-step--skipped .nd-step-btn { opacity: 0.5; }
  .nd-step--skipped .nd-step-label { text-decoration: line-through; }
</style>
